From pearl-miui-camera-6.6-compat
Subject: [PATCH] Drop null capture result safely

Some pearl capture paths deliver a null CaptureResult to the 6.6 saver.
Return empty metadata instead of dereferencing the null result and
terminating the camera process after the shutter is pressed.

---
 smali/S8/e.smali | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali/S8/e.smali b/smali/S8/e.smali
index 6fa1396..compat 100644
--- a/smali/S8/e.smali
+++ b/smali/S8/e.smali
@@ -150,6 +150,16 @@
 .method public static c(Landroid/hardware/camera2/CaptureResult;)Lxi/b;
     .registers 7
 
+    if-nez p0, :capture_result_present
+
+    new-instance v5, Lxi/b;
+
+    invoke-direct {v5}, Ljava/lang/Object;-><init>()V
+
+    return-object v5
+
+    :capture_result_present
+
     sget-object v0, Landroid/hardware/camera2/CaptureResult;->SENSOR_EXPOSURE_TIME:Landroid/hardware/camera2/CaptureResult$Key;
 
     invoke-virtual {p0, v0}, Landroid/hardware/camera2/CaptureResult;->get(Landroid/hardware/camera2/CaptureResult$Key;)Ljava/lang/Object;
